= Social Welfare

The social safety net can reduce poverty or become a political target. What do we expand?

- @child_credit: Expand the child tax credit
- @paid_leave: Paid family leave
- @housing: Build housing and loosen zoning
- @easy_discard

@child_credit
subtitle: -2 budget
unavailable-subtitle: Need 2 budget.
choose-if: budget >= 2
on-arrival: budget -= 2; working_dem += 3*(1-dissent); suburban_dem += 2*(1-dissent); minority_dem += 2*(1-dissent); inequality -= 3; month_actions += 1

Child poverty falls sharply.

@paid_leave
subtitle: -1 budget
unavailable-subtitle: Need 1 budget.
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; working_dem += 2*(1-dissent); suburban_dem += 2*(1-dissent); young_dem += 1*(1-dissent); month_actions += 1

Workers get leave to care for newborns and sick relatives.

@housing
subtitle: -1 budget
unavailable-subtitle: Need 1 budget.
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: abundance_strength += 3; budget -= 1; young_dem += 3*(1-dissent); suburban_dem -= 1*(1-dissent); inequality -= 2; economic_growth += 0.2; month_actions += 1

A housing bill makes building easier and cheaper, over local objections.
